The GR2 container implementation was developed with reference to LSLib's
LSLib/Granny/GR2/Format.cs, Reader.cs and Writer.cs at commit
6f5f6987d10d8485876b8368431c948e4dea4f83. Its MIT notice is in LSLIB-LICENSE.txt.
This project implements a deliberately smaller Python serializer, not LSLib's
Divinity/Baldur's Gate mesh export pipeline.

Optional research-only reader/codec: OpenGR2, MPL-2.0, commit
4e5edd5e98dbd69270d40a92ed94cfe16e57955a. Downloaded source and its license stay
in the ignored research cache. No OpenGR2 code is copied into the converter.
See setup_research.py for the exact source and native compiler commands.

Nexus Buddy 2 commit c42a7f6d1bac7190dec5fd27efe588db91fc24a3 has no LICENSE or
COPYING file in the inspected tree. It was inspected as behavioral reference;
no code, binaries, templates or assets from it are included or executed.

Local Civ V assets are proprietary reference data. They are not dependencies
of the writer and are not included in source control or distributable output.
